<title>USA: RailAmerica '96 earning $0.22 shr vs $0.10.</title>
<headline>RailAmerica '96 earning $0.22 shr vs $0.10.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>RAILAMERICA, INC. FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS</p>
<p>				     Fiscal Year Ended December 31,</p>
<p>						1996		  1995(a)</p>
<p> Revenue			   $25,658,241	    $25,078,104</p>
<p>Depreciation and Amortization</p>
<p>					 1,526,510		1,231,622</p>
<p> Interest Expense		  2,078,383		1,277,837</p>
<p> Provision for Income Taxes	705,405		  950,299</p>
<p>Income from Continuing Operations</p>
<p>					 1,080,437		1,126,243</p>
<p>Per Share Income from</p>
<p>  Continuing Operations		 0.22		     0.10</p>
<p>Loss from Discontinued</p>
<p>  Operations (b)		   (575,558)		(257,910)</p>
<p> Net Income			    504,879		  868,333</p>
<p>Non-Recurring Preferred</p>
<p>  Stock Dividend			    --		  666,665</p>
<p>Net Income Per Share after</p>
<p>  Preferred Stock Dividend	    0.10		     0.04</p>
<p>Wtd. Average Common Shares</p>
<p>and Common Share Equivalents</p>
<p>					 4,966,296		4,554,285</p>
<p>(a) In the fourth quarter of 1995, the Company redeemed $1,000,000 in face value of convertible preferred stock, resulting in a non-recurring deemed dividend which reduced net income available to common shareholders by $666,665, or $0.14 per share.</p>
<p>(b) In March 1997, the Company adopted a plan to discontinue its motor carrier segment. The motor carrier segments loss reduced net income by $575,558, or $0.12 per share in 1996, and $257,910, or $0.06 per share in 1995.</p>
